---
alwaysApply: true
---
Use Next.js + TypeScript.

Normalization logic must remain plain TypeScript and independent of UI.

Pipeline:

raw row
→ source-specific extraction
→ common normalization
→ validation
→ metrics
→ JSON
→ dashboard

Rules:
- preserve raw title/source identifiers
- source adapters should produce one common NormalizedProduct shape
- common unit conversion should be reused across sources
- distinguish:
  - package count
  - purchasable quantity
  - physical dimensions
  - product specifications
  - strength/dosage
- derive unit price only when denominator semantics are trustworthy
- ambiguous cases should produce warnings rather than guessed values
- keep processing deterministic and testable
- avoid premature generic frameworks or category-rule engines
- keep dashboard presentation separate from normalization